WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.370
- All right y'all we always
like to close out the hour

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.050
with something that might make you smile.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.129
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:08.620
(upbeat music and audience cheering)

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.750
Generally when you think of a bird watcher

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.190
you fully envision someone with
binoculars deep among trees.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.950
Maybe a bucket hat resting
on their head looking rad.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.860
And plenty of people, sure they
enjoy ornithology that way.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.970
That's the study of birds.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.202
I'm really intelligent.

00:00:22.202 --> 00:00:23.210
(audience laughs)

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.527
And perhaps learned
that word this morning.

00:00:25.527 --> 00:00:26.360
(Audience laughs)

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.180
But a woman in upstate New
York known as Bird Lady Drin

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.020
wanted a different experience.
Something more up-close and

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.049
more personal, so check out what she did.

00:00:34.049 --> 00:00:36.966
(orchestral music)

00:00:56.007 --> 00:00:58.215
(audience cheers)

00:00:58.215 --> 00:00:59.640
It's one way to do it.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.690
Let's get this innovative
naturist on the line.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.093
What's up Bird Lady Drin?

00:01:04.093 --> 00:01:05.214
(audience cheers)

00:01:05.214 --> 00:01:06.873
- Hello, hi. It's so good to see you.

00:01:06.873 --> 00:01:09.230
[Kelly] You are so cute.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.710
I love this so much but
before we talk about that

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:15.077
face-feeder invention, you
study birds for a living, right?

00:01:15.077 --> 00:01:16.083
[Bird Lady Drin] Absolutely.

00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.940
I am a wild bird research
technician which basically means

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.100
that I go out into the wild

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.844
I humanely capture wild
birds and I study them.

00:01:24.844 --> 00:01:25.677
- That's cool.

00:01:25.677 --> 00:01:26.840
[Bird Lady Drin] And
about a year ago I made a

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.870
TikTok account and recently I
had been tagged a whole bunch

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:34.110
of times in this video where
this guy who feeds hummingbirds

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.320
has all these contraptions on his face.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.660
And I was like, you know
what? I think I can do that.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.690
So I went downstairs and I
found the only pair of glasses

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:42.670
that I had laying around.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.780
Which were these with
these eyelashes on them.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.980
And I made this little face-feeder
and sat outside for about

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.610
45 minutes all bundled up in my blanket.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.757
And then a bird came and
I've been hooked ever since.

00:01:54.757 --> 00:01:57.420
[Kelly] Oh my God. I mean,
do you, how long does it

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.520
generally take for a
bird to do that though?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.287
Do you have to sit there for hours often?

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.470
[Bird Lady Drin] Sometimes.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:06.030
Sometimes can take any anywhere
from just a minute or two

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.660
to up to three hours.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.890
And so I sit outside in
you know, minus freezing

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.060
temperatures and I'm all bundled
up in either my blanket or

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.240
my ghillie suit that I went out and I got.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.830
And I just sit and I watch and I wait.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.270
And what you guys don't get
to see is that the birds

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:25.660
are all around me, hopping
around, talking to each other.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.800
And it's like my own
little private nature show.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.317
And so it's just, it's
amazing and I'm hooked.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.170
[Kelly] I love it.
(audience cheers)

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.460
You make me smile! Thank
you so much Bird Lady Drin!

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.834
I'm liking your posts
right now, all right?

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:39.667
[Bird Lady Drin] Thank you.
(bell dings)

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.050
[Kelly] All right, well
that's not all girl.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.610
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:45.980
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson show.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.950
They wanna celebrate
those creating fearlessly

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:48.790
just like you ma'am.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.140
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:50.973
How's that sound?

00:02:50.973 --> 00:02:52.044
(audience cheers)

00:02:52.044 --> 00:02:53.490
- Oh my gosh, thank you.

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:57.820
[Kelly] Absolutely. Thank you so much!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.123
Good luck with the birds!

